From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bharat Dintakurti <bdintakurti@nvidia.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 18:33:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] NVIDIA: SAUCE: ACPI: processor_idle: Activate hierarchical
 LPI coordination

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2167301

Hierarchical LPI domains and per-CPU idle tables can be built while
firmware remains in direct-entry mode. Switch to coordinated mode only
after every present CPU has a complete domain path and all consumers are
synchronized with CPU online state. Keep direct coordination when the
top-level _LPI container exposes _RDI, because dependency-aware selection
is not implemented here.

Make the transition atomic with respect to cpuidle, CPU hotplug, and system
sleep. Install the CPUHP, PM notifier, and syscore hooks before publishing
coordinated callbacks; roll them back if PSCI OSI activation or device
re-enablement fails. If firmware cannot return to direct mode, retain the
coordinated lifecycle and its hooks so software and firmware cannot
diverge. After physical CPU removal is published, advance the rebuild
generation so a worker that observed the transitional CPU-present mask
cannot strand the system in direct mode. Compile that post-eject
notification only when the ACPI processor driver is built in, matching the
existing built-in-only hierarchy support and avoiding a built-in ACPI
dependency on processor.ko.

Use runtime PM for normal idle and paired explicit genpd transitions for
s2idle and syscore suspend. Freeze CPU-hotplug runtime-PM callbacks during
system sleep, and suspend only consumers that were active before the
transition so CPUs already offline retain their runtime state. On
PREEMPT_RT, keep runtime shared-state entry disabled and use paired direct
transitions for CPU hotplug and system suspend.

Deactivate coordination before replacing topology resources. Reactivate it
only after a complete replacement has been validated. Propagate every
rebuild-stage failure and transient reactivation failure to the delayed
retry worker, while accepting stable activation failures as a safe return
to the direct path. If coordinated cpuidle enablement fails partway
through, disable every device enabled in that attempt before restoring
direct tables and the original enabled mask.

